  "notes": [
    "At a sabzi mandi (vegetable market), call the seller भैया (brother) or दीदी (sister). It is friendly and polite.",
    "___ कैसे दिए? (\"how did you give ___?\") is the market way to ask a price. ___ कितने के हैं? also works.",
    "Bargaining is normal at a market stall, but not in a shop with printed prices. ना at the end softens a request: थोड़ा कम कीजिए ना?",
    "ले लूँगा / ले लूँगी (I'll take) agrees with the speaker: a man says लूँगा, a woman लूँगी."
  ]
